From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 21:20:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: usb: snps,dwc3-common: Add snps,lcsr-tx-deemph

The DWC_usb31 core drives the Gen2 TxDeemph on the PIPE interface from
its LCSR_TX_DEEMPH register. On the Allwinner A733 the reset value of
that register makes Gen2 writes fail. Add a property for the value.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; the property is
accepted on the controller node and reads 00 00 34 c1 in the device
tree.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/usb/snps,dwc3-common.yaml         | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/snps,dwc3-common.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/snps,dwc3-common.yaml
index 35f2d0949871..e4fd1cba406b 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/snps,dwc3-common.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/snps,dwc3-common.yaml
@@ -214,6 +214,14 @@ properties:
       devices link at Gen1 on Allwinner A733.
     type: boolean
 
+  snps,lcsr-tx-deemph:
+    description:
+      18-bit TxDeemph value the controller drives on the PIPE interface for
+      USB 3.2 Gen2 operation (LCSR_TX_DEEMPH). When absent, the register keeps
+      its reset value.
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32
+    maximum: 0x3ffff
+
   snps,gfladj-refclk-lpm-sel-quirk:
     description:
       When set, run the SOF/ITP counter based on ref_clk.
